| PPI (lambda = 1) | Angelopoulos, Bates, Fannjiang, Jordan, Zrnic, *Prediction-powered inference*, Science 2023 (arXiv:2301.09633) | baseline |
| PPI++ (data-driven power-tuning lambda; scalar linear control variate) | Angelopoulos, Duchi, Zrnic, arXiv:2311.01453 | **strongest published baseline**; the method to beat; reference code `ppi-python==0.2.3`. Implementation property (checked in the 0.2.3 source): `ppi_mean_ci` clips the estimated λ to [0,1], so for b = Cov(Y,f)/Var(f) > 1+n/N or < 0 the packaged interval is wider than unclipped PPI++; run both arms (idea-repo#6) |
| Stratified PPI (stratify on predictor/score) | Fisch et al., arXiv:2406.04291 | closest relative of "recalibrate f using labels"; run in its post-stratified form (labels are fixed, so no allocation choice) |
| Cross-PPI | Zrnic, Candès, arXiv:2309.16598 | not a competitor (it trains the predictor on the labels, which is excluded here); its cross-fitting device is what we reuse for the fitted calibrator |
